# Lab follow-up: recover a GitHub save whose response was lost and reuse its filename when retrying.
# Request: power, join Wi-Fi, run Claude Code and Codex, and change tablets across five assembled robots.
# Baseline: no five-desk launcher or Codex adapter at this project path.
# Change: single-file local-address launcher, release-specific setup, handoff, and a two-event Codex installer.
# Checked: 360/800/1366 px, durable local choices, installer merge/retry/retarget, and both agents against a test receiver.
# Physical units, real mobile-to-host sessions, and the builder’s installed firmware still require bench verification.
# Nov 25: Owner requested a numbered overview, device and integration branches, behavior mapping, and a test.
# Before: three reference tabs. After: six navigable steps, manual/Claude/Codex paths, plus Android companion backlog #1033.
# Checked: existing controls and install gates, all branches at phone/tablet/desktop widths, remapping existing hooks,
# per-unit choices across reload, and two customized event commands reaching the test receiver.
# Test results on the wizard's last screen are the operator's observations on the selected physical unit.
# Mobile request: desktop-free control on a phone hotspot, custom commands, Bluetooth feasibility, and a phased app.
# Added a per-robot browser controller, saved gestures and timed pairs, hotspot onboarding, and roadmap in issue #1033.
# Checked regression coverage, per-robot commands, authorization and failures, plus HTTPS-to-HTTP CORS and a real POST
# against a local test receiver. Physical Samsung tethering, robot motion and Bluetooth remain unverified.
# Nov 26: separate gesture test bench, shared GitHub routine library, and active/away reader requested.
# Before: a per-browser two-gesture editor. After: 14 stock gestures across builds, five hardware checks,
# joint steps within saved calibration, optional streamed chimes, GitHub-backed routines and reading contexts.
# Browser checks cover stock requests on both firmware shapes, library persistence, conflict handling,
# active/away transitions, and the previous setup paths. Physical robot motion and locked-phone delivery need hardware.
# Nov 26: a home Wi-Fi unit received a generic connection error. Studio now offers on-device provisioning,
# the factory hostname for an unsaved first slot, a direct reachability test and permission-specific recovery.
# Optional capability failures leave stock gestures usable. Browser tests reproduce the original failure and exercise
# setup mode, denied permission, a failed gesture status check, and missing joint limits. Owner's LAN is unverified.
